WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.840
Our breathing can deepen
and become irregular.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.800
Our heart starts to race,
our pupils dilate

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.560
which might be one
of the reasons so many people

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:13.960
close their eyes during a kiss.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.360
There are three sensations

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.760
that one should really recognise
when they're kissing.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.920
First of all there's the
wonderful feeling of touch

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.880
because our lips
are extremely sensitive,

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.160
we have more nerve neurons
on the end of our lips

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.560
than any other place
in our body,

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.760
except some areas in our genitalia.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.760
And then of course
also there's taste.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.560
Each individual has
a unique taste to them

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:38.160
and some people are much better
at recognising taste than others

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.000
and then of course
there's also smell.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.400
Ovid in some of his poems
talked about kisses smelling

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.920
like ripening apples in a chest.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.920
There's a lot of theories
as to why we kiss

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.240
but some of it may have to do
with our earliest experiences

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.360
on planet Earth.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.680
When we're infants,
through being kissed by parents

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.640
and also through nursing,
through a lot of lip stimulation

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:04.000
that becomes associated through
neural pathways in our brain

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.280
with these very, very
positive emotions.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.160
And so we're building
these neural pathways

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.800
that attribute kissing and lip
stimulation with love and security

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.240
and all of these wonderful things

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.960
that later in life when we want
to express ourselves that way,

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.160
we probably do so
using our mouth.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.040
While we can't zip
ourselves back in time

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.080
and kind of discover when
and where and how the first kiss

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.240
took place among humans,

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.280
what we do know is that other species

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.360
are very attracted to the
rosy bottoms of females

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.520
when they're at peak fertility,
when they're in estrus.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.600
There are some anthropologists
that think that the lips

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.480
are what's called 'the genital echo'
so they mimic the female genitals

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:50.040
in shape, composition,
colour and texture,

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.040
and they serve as reliable indicator

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.160
of when a woman
might be ready to mate.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.040
Desmond Morris, a British zoologist,

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.920
he's actually done
some research on lipstick,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.080
showing different men
images of women's faces

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.920
asking who the most
attractive are?

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.120
And over and over and over men are
consistently choosing the women

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:12.200
who are expressing the rosiest
most coloured lips in these studies.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:15.160
So there's something that
does draw our attention to the mouth

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.960
and the colour red
is a colour that many species

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:20.880
use to exhibit this sexual signal.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.120
The earliest evidence that
we find of any kind of kissing

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:29.000
is about 2,500 maybe 3,500 years ago,
in some of the early Vedic texts

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.320
that come from India.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:35.160
It turns out that the area right
below your eyes has sebaceous glands

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.560
that produce a unique
smell for each individual.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:41.480
So these ancient Indians in northern
India were sniffing each other

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:45.320
and of course if they ran their noses
across the cheeks of each other

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.360
and then across the nose
to the other side of the cheek,

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.600
I think that occasionally
some of them slipped

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:50.920
and may have ended up on the lips

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.880
and because the lips
are so sensitive,

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.960
they may have found that that
was much more pleasurable

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.760
than just sniffing each other.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.040
The Romans can
be looked upon really as

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.240
probably the first
great kissing culture.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.920
They had different kinds of kissing.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.720
The savium was what we
might call a French kiss.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:09.880
Based on the word saliva
which we still use today

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.040
and of course they enjoyed
practicing this all the time.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.000
There's places where people just
thought kissing was disgusting

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.080
which might not be that surprising
when you consider that

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.120
for the most part, people weren’t
brushing their teeth and flossing,

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.440
using mouthwash and all
these things we do today,

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.360
where it would probably be a lot
less appetising not that long ago.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.400
However, it's something that
even where we didn’t do that

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.120
we were sniffing, we were patting,

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.200
we were licking
and sucking and nibbling

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.480
and doing things all about
each other's bodies to connect

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:44.120
and that connection is ultimately
important for keeping us together,

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.400
for keeping our bonds strong,

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.960
for raising all of the different
hormones and neurotransmitters

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:54.360
in our bodies that make us maintain
our important relationships.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.560
And kissing is a big part of that.

